Jennie from BLACKPINK!

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.309
It was cool.

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.443
When I watched the trailer

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.212
I thought

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:35.415
Wow, so that's how BLACKPINK

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:39.586
became the world
famous girl group.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.188
All because of
their hard work.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:43.823
Then I became their fan.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.191
He recommended it to me,

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.026
so I watched it.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:50.163
I have a couple of 
great documentaries

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.298
that I want to recommend.

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.733
&lt;i&gt;Don't F**k with Cats.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.301
I think it captures

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:56.703
the viewer's attention
really well.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.738
It was more powerful

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.673
that reading the article.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.843
It was very shocking.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.379
&lt;i&gt;Michael Jordan:&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;The Last Dance.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.513
As I watched that

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.149
I was amazed at

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.518
how they directed everything

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.621
so well while handling

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:15.688
all kind of emotions.

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.557
It's a beautiful
show for sure.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:20.159
My favourite documentary is

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:23.296
&lt;i&gt;Headspace: Guide to Sleep.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:24.397
That's the title.

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:25.832
When I can't sleep,

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:29.002
I follow their
guided meditation.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.837
Before I know, I'm asleep.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.772
It's so helpful!

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.774
So I recommend that.

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:38.978
&lt;i&gt;Explain &lt;/i&gt;is a series
of short documentaries.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.613
There are a lot of topics.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.116
Sound, skin, stock markets.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.984
I think it's
a documentary that

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.819
makes us question
about things.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.956
It definitely made me
question things

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.824
that I normally wouldn't.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.593
I look it up if I'm curious.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.428
And talk about it
with my friends.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.764
I think it's very
inspirational.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.565
&lt;i&gt;Peaky Blinders.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.567
It's a TV series.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.770
It's about the Shelby
family in England

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.538
just after WWI.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.607
The gangster
family gradually

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:12.245
takes over
the political world.

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:14.547
I liked the colour,
the background,

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.149
the trauma behind
the characters

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.685
and how the actors

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.620
play out their characters.

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:23.256
The outfits,
the art direction

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:26.092
about that era was
really beautiful.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:27.427
There was a lot
to learn from

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.828
so I really adore the show.

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:30.563
The filming staff

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.098
also recommended
&lt;i&gt;Peaky Blinders.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:33.566
He really likes

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:36.502
Cillian Murphy

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:37.904
so I got into it, too.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:41.741
My favourite…

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.309
I love them all.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.811
I recently watched &lt;i&gt;D.P.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.947
I served in the army, too.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.148
I wasn't a D.P. but

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:50.783
I was an MP.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.685
When I was in the army

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:54.687
it wasn't as bad
as the show but

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:58.191
it must have been like that
for the people before me.

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.693
It made me angry and upset.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.662
Watching the stories

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.197
about the runaway soldiers,

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:05.498
I related myself to them.

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:06.466
It was therapeutic.

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:07.667
I loved Cho
Hyun-cheol's acting

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.202
I debuted with &lt;i&gt;China Town&lt;/i&gt;.

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.938
And he played Hong-joo

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:13.706
I loved him there, too.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:14.841
And in &lt;i&gt;D.P.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:16.676
He was an otaku
Private First Class.

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:19.946
Later in the show,
he totally changed

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.247
and it was very impactful.

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.883
I think if you have Netflix,

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.752
you probably watched and
enjoyed &lt;i&gt;Money Heist.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:30.056
I got into Netflix because
of &lt;i&gt;Money Heist &lt;/i&gt;in a way.

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:32.558
Season 5 will be out soon.
I'm looking forward to it.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.061
So excited.

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:36.963
I'm a big fan
of &lt;i&gt;Money Heist.&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:39.866
It's such an honour and
I'm super nervous.

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:42.668
In the original version,
Berlin is kind of chic

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:45.037
and cold-blooded.

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:47.240
He's on the verge
of good and evil.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.909
But in the Korean version,

00:06:49.976 --> 00:06:52.345
Berlin has a good
reason to be like that.

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:55.014
So it'll be
completely different.

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:57.183
I wanted to
portray Berlin as

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.851
a real human being.

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:00.787
So it'll be very different
from the original.

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.355
My favourite is

00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:04.757
&lt;i&gt;Roma.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:06.959
I think it was after I got

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:09.562
casted for &lt;i&gt;Squid Game.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:12.632
It was her first time acting
as the heroine of Roma.

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:16.202
So I got comforted
from her acting.

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:18.504
When I'm feeling tired

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:20.606
or when I'm feeling lost,

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:23.376
I go back to the show
to refresh myself.

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.511
So I'd like to
recommend this show.

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:29.615
I think you guys
are into mysteries.

00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:32.418
There's a show called &lt;i&gt;Dark.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:34.253
It's really interesting
and the subject is unique.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:38.157
The story starts with the
disappearance of a child.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:41.994
This is not a spoiler.

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:43.029
It's not?

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:45.331
The story develops
as they uncover

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:48.401
the secrets they've been
hiding from each other.

00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:52.438
Which ends up destroying
the whole town.

00:07:52.505 --> 00:07:55.041
It's so interesting
I couldn't stop watching.

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.342
&lt;i&gt;-Dark.&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;-Dark.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:58.911
I heard this recently.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.146
